WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.820
So Ra No Wo To

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.830
Rio-sempai!

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.060
Good work!

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.170
Find it?

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.960
Yeah, we got it!

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.970
You can find anything here.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:02.810
It's so warm!

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.000
I feel so much better.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:11.480
But, Rio-sempai, were you
on yard duty today?

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.570
There was something
I wanted to burn.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.040
It's been six months since Kanata
came to the fortress.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.090
She's gotten pretty good.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.130
She has a good teacher.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.650
Ow. That's hot.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:45.680
I guess I can finally put
away those earplugs...

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:54.390
Hey, madam, shouldn't you
stay in town this winter?

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.840
I'm fine.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:00.950
I won't kick the bucket that easy.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:08.950
I've been living alone on this
mountain for fifty years.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:13.960
A Departure - The First Snow

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:19.720
Go. Go. Go. Stop!

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.090
It's finally starting to
look like a real tank.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.140
You can take care of the rest
yourself, right, Noël?

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.890
Yes. I'm happy.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.090
Then let's go get some tea.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:32.070
Yeah.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:40.960
Hey, Kureha-chan...

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.320
Huh?

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.290
Where did it go?

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.630
It should be here...

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:52.380
Oh, my. What's wrong?

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:55.240
The army almanac is
around here, isn't it?

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:59.490
Kanata wanted to know
about Princess Iliya.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.190
I'm sorry.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:05.090
If it isn't there, I can't help you.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:06.920
Darn...

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.530
Naomi-san might have one!

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.450
I'll ask her next time we see her.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:13.230
OK!

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:28.990
Princess Iliya is the eldest daughter
of the current Archduke Arkadia.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:35.970
I think I already told you,
but she's a really famous tanker!

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:39.920
Claus-san was saying things would be
different if she were alive.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:46.150
Yeah, she passed away.
Hmm, about two years ago...

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.820
In the war?

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.270
No.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:54.310
She was assigned to
the royal guard,

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:59.230
but military parades and stuff were also part of
her job, so she'd travel around the country.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:05.880
On her way to a city, she tried to save
a child drowning in a river...

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.370
But I feel relieved.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.870
It's just a rumor, but...

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.630
Iliya...

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:23.820
Kanata-san!

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:28.470
Yumina-san, and...

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.970
Um, it's Kanata.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:49.450
Um...Yumina-san...uh,
brought Yuuko-chan...

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:58.310
Yuuko-chan is the daughter of Martin-san
and, um, a lady named Jacott...

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:02.200
She lives alone in
the mountains...

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:05.210
I sometimes buy vegetables and
stuff from her at the market.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:09.510
Oh, I know! You said you liked
those pickled vegetables, right?

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:13.570
She's the one who made them.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:19.560
Anyway, uh, lately
no one's seen her,

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:24.580
and she's kind of frail,
so they're worried.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:28.730
She lives deep in the mountains,

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:29.960
and...

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:32.030
Fine! Fine!

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.760
I'll listen to what you have to say,
so wait just a second.

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:38.160
OK!

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.790
People were saying

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:45.550
she was going to marry
the emperor

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:49.260
of the holy city, Rome, to improve
relations with them.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:52.290
But she'd have been
his third wife!

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.770
<i>The third!</i>

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:56.920
No way, right?

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.640
So basically, she'd have
been a hostage, right?

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:05.520
But that stopped once she died,

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:10.580
and we fought them until
this year's peace treaty.

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:16.540
Geez, we're finally here...

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:20.040
A newly built house?

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:24.130
Didn't she supposedly live alone?

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.790
That's what I heard.

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:36.680
Madam!

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:41.850
I see... Yuuko sent you.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:42.700
Yes.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.980
She's such a kind girl.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:51.080
She's too good for that
runny-nosed Martin.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.200
This is a really nice house.

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:55.290
Thank you.

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:58.970
I built this house.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:00.550
Wow!

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:04.460
Then what about that
one over there?

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:08.030
It was for my son...

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:10.200
You have a son?

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:17.100
He lives in a far away city now,
but I keep it ready for him.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:23.600
I have to keep it nice and
clean, so my son and them

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.520
can use it whenever they want.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:43.000
When will your son
be home, madam?

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:45.250
He'll be here soon.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:47.990
Winter is what's coming soon.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:51.440
You should leave the mountain
before the first snow.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:53.260
I can't.

00:08:55.280 --> 00:09:00.860
I have to finish that house.

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:05.420
I won't leave for any reason
until it's done.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:06.320
But...

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.730
Don't be stupid!

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.030
Are you ready for winter?

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:11.010
Do you have firewood?

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:12.290
Provisions?

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.240
You're not ready at all!

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:18.090
It will work out.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:22.340
Thanks for worrying, ladies.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:25.370
Madam!

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:35.370
What a stubborn old lady!

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:39.280
She's just like you, I bet.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:40.900
Quiet.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:42.460
Why would I...

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.130
Sometimes you won't listen
to anyone else, either,

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:47.140
even when you know you should.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.400
Shut up!

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:56.000
Hey, that letter...
Why show it to me?

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:02.220
I heard this in last week's
communications,

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:07.660
but the Roman army on the Eastern
border has started moving.

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:34.680
So these are for old
lady Jacott, huh?

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:38.000
OK! Take these, too!

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.430
Thank you!

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:40.700
By the way,

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:44.450
do you know what's going on
with the peace talks?

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:47.810
I... I'm sorry.

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:50.370
If only Princess Iliya
were still alive...

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:56.520
By the way, Martin, didn't Iliya-sama
have a younger sister?

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.550
And your 4,000,000 change!

00:10:58.550 --> 00:10:59.720
That's the first I've heard of it.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:05.950
Well, she's not really a legitimate child,
so no one talks about it.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:09.350
She's third in line to the
throne or something.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:12.600
Um, that little sister...

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:20.990
Bye!

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:22.360
Thanks!

00:11:23.590 --> 00:11:24.620
Thank you.

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:30.620
Want to take a walk?

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:33.630
Hey, Kanata...

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:37.760
What kind of place was the village
where you were born?

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.630
Just a normal country village.

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:48.500
There were fields and goats and cows,
but not many people.

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:51.640
It's not like this place.

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:54.270
But it was a nice place, I bet.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.600
And you had good parents.

00:11:57.600 --> 00:11:59.280
I can tell by looking at you.

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:03.530
What kind of place did
you grow up in?

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:15.500
I grew up in a small village near the capital,
with pretty lakes and forests.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:20.680
I lived there with my mom.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:25.260
It was boring. Nothing ever happened.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:33.230
My one comfort was my sister,
who loved me very much.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:38.820
She was only my half-sister, but she would
come and play with me sometimes.

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:41.510
I always looked up to her.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:44.810
She was beautiful and kind.

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:48.200
And she accepted her
fate with pride.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.920
I learned the trumpet from her.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:59.420
But she was too kind...
And that became her undoing.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:05.470
The first time I came here,
I thought this town was like a labyrinth.

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:16.730
I got lost and ended up here,
but I felt like I'd finally reached my goal.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:25.990
But I noticed later, that this
was just a dead end.

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:29.780
That's not true!

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:34.750
I get lost all the time.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:38.240
But I like to get lost!

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:44.310
Who cares if you were lost?!
Or if it's a dead end?!

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:50.930
That's how I met you!

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:01.320
At times, I'm jealous
of you, Kanata.

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:10.570
If only I could be so
true to myself.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.980
This'll do it.

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:35.100
Why are you so worried
about me?

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:40.100
You remind me of my mother.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:45.110
I never had a pretty girl like you.

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:49.600
I was born from a forbidden love.

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:55.830
My mother always waited for him.
He might come by once a year.

00:14:55.830 --> 00:15:01.130
And then she died,
still living unhappily like that.

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:06.630
Why do you think that
she was unhappy?

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:07.980
But-

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:09.610
I'm quite happy here.

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:16.690
He promised he'd come back.

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:19.560
He promised he'd come get me.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.840
For me, that's enough.

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:22.860
But...

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:27.960
What else could I have done?

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.430
That's right.

00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:33.440
If there had been something else
I could've done, I might have.

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:35.320
But you know...

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:38.210
Is that enough for you?

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:40.000
Are you really happy?

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:44.740
Because I have my memories of them.

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:50.490
I have my memories of them
and the hope that I will see them again.

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:53.330
That's enough.

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:54.970
It's more than enough.

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:10.010
I thought it was getting cold.

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:33.500
It was on a snowy night like
this that I first met you...

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:47.640
When Madam was young,
Seize was a famous resort city.

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:09.740
She fell in love with a young man
who was a rich merchant's heir.

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:23.310
And soon, she came to bear his child.
But he already had a family.

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:29.150
For good or ill, the man's own
wife never had a child,

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:34.670
so he took her child
and went home.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:42.720
He promised he'd someday
come for her.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:15.530
Now that I'm old, I sometimes
think to myself... What if...

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:23.620
Life is losing things,
one after another.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:27.290
But to have lost, you must
first have gained.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:34.040
And the greater your joy at your gain,
the greater your sorrow at your loss. But...

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:44.430
But if you have the memories
of your happiness...

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:49.430
With those memories, you can live on.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:56.250
Oh, right.

00:18:56.250 --> 00:19:01.260
This may not be the time, but I found that
picture of Princess Iliya you wanted.

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:02.120
Naomi-san!

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:04.990
Filicia, it's OK.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.880
I guess it would be from
five years ago,

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.850
when she visited Seize.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:16.170
Is that Shuko?

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:29.390
Rio-sempai!

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:32.580
I think my parents wanted me to marry
and inherit the household.

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:38.590
But I was entranced by the
sound of that trumpet.

00:20:39.890 --> 00:20:42.590
And I couldn't forget it.

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:47.480
That was Iliya-san, wasn't it?

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:52.480
I knew it. You met her, too.

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:58.480
Her music welled up within me.
It was so wonderful.

00:20:59.010 --> 00:21:02.990
And you and I met.

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:09.870
I think I ran away to this town,

00:21:10.220 --> 00:21:13.370
so at first, I didn't care.

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:17.630
I knew I would leave someday.

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:24.270
But now, I don't really
want to leave.

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:28.870
That's probably why I have to go,

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:31.390
to do what I can.

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:35.650
To do what only I can do.

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:43.700
I won't say goodbye.

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:50.030
No matter how far away you are...

00:21:51.630 --> 00:21:54.040
...sound fills the air.

00:21:54.440 --> 00:21:56.770
Sound fills the air...

00:21:56.770 --> 00:22:00.710
...and reaches people's hearts.

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:07.800
Kanata, was I a good
teacher to you?

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:11.740
Yes.

00:22:26.390 --> 00:22:31.670
Thus, Rio-sempai left us.

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:37.760
Leaving behind a music that
I would hear forever,

00:22:37.760 --> 00:22:42.560
a wonderful, wonderful
sound of the sky.

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:19.890
A Visitor - A Burning Field of Snow

00:24:16.020 --> 00:24:16.880
Next time:

00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:17.930
A Visitor.

00:24:17.930 --> 00:24:19.320
A Burning Field of Snow.

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:24.890
This program is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to people, parties,
or situations is purely coincidental.
